Here are 25 patterns and the problems they help solve:

1. Load balancing → Uneven server traffic → High-traffic APIs, checkout systems

2. Caching → Repeated expensive reads → News feeds, product catalogues

3. CDN → Slow global delivery → Video streaming, image hosting

4. Database sharding → One database cannot scale → Messages, user activity

5. Replication → Availability and read scale → Catalogues, reporting systems

6. Consistent hashing → Excessive data movement → Distributed caches, storage nodes

7. Batch processing → Large scheduled workloads → Billing, daily analytics

8. Stream processing → Real-time event handling → Fraud detection, live tracking

9. Message queues → Sudden traffic spikes → Emails, video processing

10. Publish-subscribe → Many consumers need updates → Alerts, live scores

11. Event-driven architecture → Tightly coupled services → Orders, ride tracking

12. CQRS → Different read-write demands → Ledgers, order histories

13. Event sourcing → Complete change history → Transactions, audit logs

14. Saga pattern → Cross-service transactions → Travel booking, food delivery

15. Transactional outbox → Database updated, event lost → Payments, order notifications

16. Idempotency → Duplicate actions during retries → Payments, webhook processing

17. Rate limiting → Too many requests → Login attempts, public APIs

18. Circuit breaker → Failing downstream dependency → Payments, recommendation services

19. Retry with backoff → Temporary service failures → External APIs, cloud storage

20. Backpressure → Consumers cannot keep up → Log ingestion, streaming analytics

21. Leader election → Multiple nodes competing → Schedulers, partition ownership

22. Distributed locking → Conflicting concurrent updates → Seat booking, inventory

23. Fan-out strategies → Distributing updates at scale → Social feeds, notifications

24. Search indexing → Slow text discovery → Product search, document search

25. Geospatial indexing → Finding nearby entities → Drivers, restaurants, deliveries